            <header class="lesson-header"><span class="lesson-number">Lesson 18</span><h1>Kubernetes Fundamentals</h1><div class="lesson-meta"><span class="lesson-duration"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>35 min</span><span class="lesson-level advanced">Advanced</span></div></header>
            <div class="lesson-body">
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Core Concepts</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Pod:</strong> Smallest deployable unit (1+ containers)</li>
                        <li><strong>Deployment:</strong> Manages replica sets and rolling updates</li>
                        <li><strong>Service:</strong> Stable network endpoint for pods</li>
                        <li><strong>Ingress:</strong> External access to services (HTTP/HTTPS)</li>
                        <li><strong>Namespace:</strong> Virtual cluster for isolation</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Architecture</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-text">┌────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                 Cluster                    │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │            Control Plane             │  │
│  │  API Server | Scheduler | etcd       │  │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────┘  │
│                                            │
│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐         │
│  │   Node 1    │  │   Node 2    │  ...    │
│  │ ┌─────────┐ │  │ ┌─────────┐ │         │
│  │ │   Pod   │ │  │ │   Pod   │ │         │
│  │ └─────────┘ │  │ └─────────┘ │         │
│  └─────────────┘  └─────────────┘         │
└────────────────────────────────────────────┘</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>kubectl Commands</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-bash"># Get resources
kubectl get pods
kubectl get services
kubectl get deployments

# Apply configuration
kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml

# View logs
kubectl logs pod-name -f

# Execute in pod
kubectl exec -it pod-name -- /bin/sh

# Describe resource
kubectl describe pod pod-name</code></pre>
                </section>

                <LessonTakeaways>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Kubernetes orchestrates containerized applications.</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Pods are the smallest deployable unit.</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Services provide stable networking.</LessonTakeaway>
                </LessonTakeaways>
            </div>
